input.findings:
## Summary of the defects found

Four different "margin geometries" coexist today:

1. `labelLayoutHelper.prepareLabelLayoutInfo` applies `textMargin` to the **local** rect but `minMargin` to the **global** rect — so `minMargin` is silently dropped from the OBB (`obb` is built from `localRect`+`transform`), i.e. rotated labels lose `minMargin` in `hideOverlap`/`labelIntersect`.
2. `chart/pie/labelLayout.ts` reads `label.style.margin` as a raw number in two places. With `textMargin` (array) this evaluates to a string concat → `NaN` → every outer pie label ends up hidden. It also inflates only the height, and calls `getBoundingRect()` before `getComputedTransform()` (opposite of the documented order).
3. `shiftLayoutOnX/Y` move `label.x/y` and `rect`, but leave `localRect`/`transform`/`obb` stale, so the `hideOverlap` that runs right after in `LabelManager.layout` uses pre-shift OBBs. The same staleness exists after `adjustBreakLabelPair` moves break labels.
4. `labelStyle.ts` lets the internal `opt.defaultTextMargin` override an explicit user `minMargin` (this makes `axis.nameTextStyle.minMargin` a complete no-op today).

---

## 1) `src/label/labelLayoutHelper.ts`

