        if (!isLabelInside) {
            // NOTE: Get bounding rect after getComputedTransform, or label may not been
            // updated by the host el. (Same convention as `label/labelLayoutHelper.ts`.)
            const labelTransform = label.getComputedTransform();
            const textRect = label.getBoundingRect().clone();
            textRect.applyTransform(labelTransform);
            const verticalMargin = getLabelVerticalMargin(label);
            textRect.y -= verticalMargin[0];
            textRect.height += verticalMargin[0] + verticalMargin[1];
```

Backward compatibility check: with no margin declared, `getLabelVerticalMargin` returns `[1.05, 1.05]` → `y -= 1.05; height += 2.1`, identical to today. With `minMargin: m`, it returns `[m/2 + 1.05, m/2 + 1.05]` → `y -= (m + 2.1)/2; height += m + 2.1`, also identical to today. Only the broken `textMargin`-array path changes behaviour.

`unconstrainedWidth: textRect.width` (line 528) and `realTextWidth = layout.rect.width + extraPaddingH` (line 232) stay correct because horizontal margin is intentionally not folded into `rect.width`.

### 3e. Related bug in the same file (line 493)

```ts
        hasLabelRotate = !!labelRotate;
```

`hasLabelRotate` is declared once outside `data.each` (line 347: `let hasLabelRotate = false;`) but assigned (not accumulated) per data item, so only the **last** sector decides whether `avoidOverlap` runs (line 547: `if (!hasLabelRotate && seriesModel.get('avoidLabelOverlap'))`). With per-item `label.rotate`, `avoidOverlap` can run on rotated labels, where `layout.rect` (a transformed AABB) is mixed with local rects in `constrainTextWidth`. Correct fix:

```ts
        hasLabelRotate = hasLabelRotate || !!labelRotate;
```

Flag this to the reviewer as a behaviour change (`avoidLabelOverlap` will now be skipped in more mixed-rotation cases) — it can be landed separately if you want to keep the margin change isolated.

