## 4) `src/label/labelStyle.ts`

Current (lines 457-470):

```ts
    const minMargin = textStyleModel.get('minMargin');
    if (minMargin != null) {
        textStyle.margin = minMargin;
        (textStyle as LabelExtendedTextStyle).__marginType = LabelMarginType.minMargin;
    }
    const textMargin = textStyleModel.get('textMargin');
    if (textMargin != null) {
        textStyle.margin = clone(textMargin);
        (textStyle as LabelExtendedTextStyle).__marginType = LabelMarginType.textMargin;
    }
    else if (opt.defaultTextMargin != null) {
        textStyle.margin = clone(opt.defaultTextMargin);
        (textStyle as LabelExtendedTextStyle).__marginType = LabelMarginType.textMargin;
    }
```

Bug: when `textMargin` is absent but `opt.defaultTextMargin` is present, the internal default overrides an explicit user `minMargin`. `AxisBuilder.ts:930-937` always passes a non-null `defaultTextMargin` for the axis name (`DEFAULT_CENTER_NAME_MARGIN_LEVELS = [[1,2],[5,3],[8,3]]`, `DEFAULT_ENDS_NAME_MARGIN_LEVELS = [[0,1],[0,3],[0,3]]`), so `axis.nameTextStyle.minMargin` is currently a complete no-op.

Replacement:

```ts
    // Priority: explicit `textMargin` > explicit `minMargin` > internal `opt.defaultTextMargin`.
    const minMargin = textStyleModel.get('minMargin');
    const textMargin = textStyleModel.get('textMargin');
    if (textMargin != null) {
        textStyle.margin = clone(textMargin);
        (textStyle as LabelExtendedTextStyle).__marginType = LabelMarginType.textMargin;
    }
    else if (minMargin != null) {
        textStyle.margin = minMargin;
        (textStyle as LabelExtendedTextStyle).__marginType = LabelMarginType.minMargin;
    }
    else if (opt.defaultTextMargin != null) {
        textStyle.margin = clone(opt.defaultTextMargin);
        (textStyle as LabelExtendedTextStyle).__marginType = LabelMarginType.textMargin;
    }
```

No import changes. `useStyle(normalStyle)` at `labelStyle.ts:289` always installs a brand new style object, so `__marginType` never leaks across renders — nothing else needed there.

