## 7) `src/util/layout.ts` — reviewed, no functional change required

`getLayoutRect`'s `margin` (declared at lines 274-285, applied at 287-384, stored as `rect.margin` at line 384) is a *component padding* concept (`legend.padding`, `title.padding`, ...), unrelated to label margin. Do not merge it with the label margin rules.

`positionElement` (lines 588-603) is the only `getBoundingRect`/`getLocalTransform` site here:

```ts
    let rect;
    if (boundingMode === 'raw') {
        rect = el.type === 'group'
            ? new BoundingRect(0, 0, +positionInfo.width || 0, +positionInfo.height || 0)
            : el.getBoundingRect();
    }
    else {
        rect = el.getBoundingRect();
        if (el.needLocalTransform()) {
            const transform = el.getLocalTransform();
            // Notice: raw rect may be inner object of el,
            // which should not be modified.
            rect = rect.clone();
            rect.applyTransform(transform);
        }
    }
```

It uses the **local** transform (by design: box layout is within the parent space) and never sees `__marginType`, but its only callers (`Breadcrumb.ts:107`, `GraphicView.ts:340`, `ToolboxView.ts:312`, `VisualMapView.ts:158`) position groups / `graphic` elements whose styles do not go through `createTextStyle`, so no label carries `__marginType` here. Recommended: add a one-line comment pointing at `labelLayoutHelper` so the two `margin` concepts are not conflated. Importing `label/*` into `util/layout.ts` would introduce a new module dependency and is not worth it.

